    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a1">

                <pb facs="0650" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg436"/>

                <head>Correspondence with Lord Lyons respecting his departure from Paris, and
                    provision made for the withdrawal of British subjects.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">Lord Lyons to Earl Granville</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 26, 1870</date>. (Received August
                    27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith to
                    your lordship, extracted from the “Journal Officiel” of this day, a decree of
                    the governor of Paris concerning the expulsion of persons without the means of
                    subsistence.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d223-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d223-a1-a1"/>
